Remember our cheat sheet:

LL → RIGHT
RR → LEFT

LR → LEFT + RIGHT
RL → RIGHT + LEFT

We actually only need to write two rotation functions.

Because LR and RL are combinations of these two.

Right rotation

Imagine:

      y
     /
    x
   /
  T1

Right rotation around y gives:

      x
     / \
   T1   y

Code:

struct Node* rightRotate(struct Node *y)
{
    struct Node *x = y->left;
    struct Node *T2 = x->right;

    x->right = y;
    y->left = T2;

    return x;
}
Just understand these three lines:

x = y->left;
T2 = x->right;

Then:

x->right = y;
y->left = T2;
